venus 0111: present the iPhone X canvas (1125x2436 @3x) on the 1440x3200 panel

The userland renders at the "canvas" size (the /arm-io/disp0 canvas-width /
canvas-height properties, the same ones IOMobileFramebuffer.framework reads)
and asks the kernel for the display size (user client selector 8,
GetDisplaySize).  Both have to be the same size: the framework builds the
render target from the canvas and the display mode (and with it the point
size = pixel size / /chosen display-scale) from GetDisplaySize.  When they
disagree, backboardd swaps empty frames - a black panel, no crash, no clue
(that is what the 750x1334 canvas on venus was).

The canvas is now 1125x2436 (375x812 points at 3x = a real iPhone screen,
the iPhone X presentation upstream sweet uses; 1440x3200 at 2x would be
720x1600 points, which no iPhone has).  The panel (the ABL splash memory,
boot_args.Video) stays 1440x3200: the canvas is scaled up to fill it
(nearest neighbour, the inverse mapping, so every panel pixel is written).
sweetfb_letterbox=1 draws the canvas 1:1 centered instead, sweetfb_native=1
presents the real panel size (1440x3200) as before.

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -86,6 +86,19 @@
 #define SWEET_FB_LOGICAL_W              1125
 #define SWEET_FB_LOGICAL_H              2436
